---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { links } from "../site";
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="Imagory the app is fully offline with no telemetry. This website uses cookieless Vercel Web Analytics.">
  <section class="section container">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lead">The app never connects to the internet. This website counts visits, without cookies.</p>
      <p class="muted">Last updated 12 November 2026.</p>

      <h2>The app</h2>
      <p>Imagory is fully offline. Your photos and everything the app learns about them stay on your computer.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>No telemetry, no accounts, no update checks, and no network calls of any kind.</li>
        <li>It never modifies, moves or deletes your photos. It only reads them.</li>
        <li>It writes only to its own library folder (<code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Imagory</code> on Windows, <code>~/.local/share/imagory</code> on Linux) and to a cleanup output folder that you pick yourself.</li>
        <li>Logs are written to the library folder and stay on your computer.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>The site is hosted on Vercel. It sets no cookies, shows no ads, and has no newsletter.</p>
      <p>It uses <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy">Vercel Web Analytics</a>. According to Vercel, it is cookieless and does not use personal identifiers. It counts page views, referrers, country, and browser, operating system and device type.</p>
      <p>Downloads are counted as visits to <a href="/download/windows">/download/windows</a> and <a href="/download/linux">/download/linux</a>. That is the only way the site knows a download was started.</p>
      <p>The files themselves are downloaded from GitHub, not from this site. GitHub's own <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">privacy statement</a> applies to that download.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about privacy? Open an issue on <a href={links.issues}>GitHub</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
